> //   (1) --form now fills the field with the PER-KEY key-event trace instead
> //       of Input.insertText: the same real mouse click INTO the field focuses
> //       it, then for EVERY nonce character the runner dispatches a real
> //       Input.dispatchKeyEvent keyDown (text/unmodifiedText/key/code/
> //       windowsVirtualKeyCode derived per character: digits -> Digit<N> + VK
> //       48+N, letters -> Key<X> + VK 65+, hyphen -> Minus + VK 189) followed
> //       by the matching keyUp — 2n key events for an n-character nonce — and
> //       reads the field's DOM value back after EACH keystroke. The receipt's
> //       journey.form.typing[] is the per-key prefix trace: entry i records the
> //       character, its derived code/VK and the DOM value after keystroke i,
> //       which must equal the nonce prefix of length i+1 (per-key delivery
> //       witness: exactly one character per keystroke, in order, no dropped or
> //       duplicated keys). journey.form.keyEventCount records the dispatched
> //       event count; valueBeforeFirstKey must be empty; the value after the
> //       full trace must equal the invocation-bound nonce; the submission and
> //       its witnesses (form-page nonce marker, rendered echo page, fixture
> //       server's served log) are the r51 chain unchanged.
> //   (2) S153's Input.dispatchKeyEvent description is the round's located
> //       source ground (re-opened byte-identical this round; the r51
> //       insertText/dispatchMouseEvent ground carries the click and the prior
> //       fill mechanism).
> //   (3) The runtime contract is unchanged: --runtime MUST be passed
> //       explicitly (auto-update drift is the standing host condition); the
> //       nonce/profile/token prefixes move to tabi-r52 so cross-generation
> //       receipts refuse by shape.
